# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# These are URLs from the academy's previous website. They are still in Google's
# index, still on old flyers, and still being crawled: Search Console reports
# eight of them returning 404. A 404 throws away whatever standing the URL had;
# a 301 hands it to the page that replaced it.
#
# The current site is one page with anchors, so most of these land on a section
# of the homepage rather than a page of their own. That is the honest mapping:
# the content still exists, it just lives further down.

/plans-and-pricing              /pricing            301
/contact-us                     /#contact           301
/summer-camp                    /programs/summer-camp-fulshear   301
/2nd-annniversary-celebration   /                   301
/sauna-cold-plunge-dashboard    /                   301

# Old Wix-era links to the business name itself (Search Console reports /Labyrinth as a 404). Path matching is
# case sensitive, so both spellings are listed; neither has a page of its own, so both go home.
/Labyrinth                      /                   301
/labyrinth                      /                   301

# Wix leftovers. `fera.admin.js` was a review-app asset on the old platform and
# `/1/1` is a stray gallery path; neither has an equivalent, so both go home
# rather than 404.
/assets/public/*                /                   301
/1/1                            /                   301

# Common guesses at pages this site does not have, so a mistyped or misremembered
# URL lands somewhere useful instead of on the 404 page.
#
# /programs is no longer one of them. It used to 301 to a fragment of the front
# page; it is now a real page with a page of its own for each program under it,
# so the rule is gone and Cloudflare serves programs/index.html directly. A
# redirect rule here would win over that file, which is why removing it is the
# whole job. /classes still redirects, because it is a guess rather than a URL
# we publish.
/classes                        /programs/          301
/contact                        /#contact           301
/faq                            /#faq               301
/class-schedule                 /schedule           301
/plans                          /pricing            301
/instructors                    /coaches/           301
/free-trial                     /#contact           301
/trial                          /#contact           301

# A short link for the Rolling for Ribbons fundraiser, for posts, print and word of mouth. It lands on the
# donation section of the seminar page (the live progress bar and the amount buttons), not on the bare Stripe
# link, so people see how close the goal is. A 302, because the campaign ends and the target may change.
/donate                         /self-defense-for-women#donate   302

# labyrinth.vision/ennova is printed on the resident card. The QR code carries
# the exact URL, but anybody typing it off the card is reading a proper noun and
# will reasonably capitalise it. Path matching here is case sensitive, so /Ennova
# would 404 on the one page whose whole audience arrives from print.
/Ennova                         /ennova             301
/ENNOVA                         /ennova             301

# Cloudflare Pages already serves /blog/<slug> for /blog/<slug>.html via a 308.
# Those .html URLs are in Google's index from the old sitemap, so they are named
# explicitly as 301s. A permanent redirect is what tells Google to move the
# indexing to the new URL, which a 308 does not do as clearly.
/blog/:slug.html                /blog/:slug         301
